{
  "title": "Longest Palindromic Substring",
  "description": "A *palindrome* reads the same forwards and backwards. Given a string `s`, return its longest substring that is a palindrome. A substring is a run of consecutive characters.\n\nIf several palindromes share the longest length, return the one that **starts earliest** in `s`.\n\n### Constraints\n\n- `1 <= s.size() <= 1000`\n- `s` contains only lowercase English letters and digits.\n- Inputs are passed as function arguments and the answer is returned from the function. Do not read from standard input or print the result.\n",
  "reference": "string longest_palindrome(string s) {\n    int n = s.size(), best_start = 0, best_length = 1;\n    for (int center = 0; center < n; ++center) {\n        for (int width = 0; width < 2; ++width) {\n            int left = center, right = center + width;\n            while (left >= 0 && right < n && s[left] == s[right]) {\n                --left;\n                ++right;\n            }\n            int length = right - left - 1;\n            int start = left + 1;\n            if (length > best_length || (length == best_length && start < best_start)) {\n                best_length = length;\n                best_start = start;\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    return s.substr(best_start, best_length);\n}\n",
  "template": "string longest_palindrome(string s) {\n    // Return the longest palindromic substring, preferring the earliest one.\n    return \"\";\n}\n",
  "tags": [
    "Strings",
    "Two Pointers",
    "Dynamic Programming"
  ],
  "examples": [
